  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound (1R,3S)-1,2,2,3-tetramethylcyclopentane-1-carboxylic acid may interact with NQO1 protein through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of Eriodictyol 7,3',4'-trimethyl ether and Miquelianin, both of which are known to modulate NQO1 activity. Additionally, the compound is linked to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 1-10, which is a target of two different compounds that also target NQO1. This indicates that the compound may influence NQO1 through a series of intermediate targets, possibly via metabolic or enzymatic pathways. The evidence suggests a potential role for the compound in regulating NQO1 activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
